English Interview Script & Preparation

Opening / Icebreaker

"Last time, I was nervous, so I didn't answer well. I hope I will do much better."

Question 1: Introduce yourself & experience

Interviewer: "Can you introduce yourself and your experience?"

Your Answer:

"Let me introduce myself. I'm Cuong, or you can call me Coby. I have worked as a software engineer at FPT software for 3 years. I have experience with C#, React, and I worked a lot with the OutSystems low-code platform. In my projects, I take care of almost the whole process: I analyze requirements, write code, test, and maintain the system. Currently, I am working as an AI engineer on a .NET project. I use AI to do most of the tasks, which helps me work much faster. That's all."

Question 2: Difficulties & Solutions

Interviewer: "Have you faced any limitations or difficulties? Can you share it with me, and what did you do to resolve these problems?"

Your Answer:

"Yes, in the past, I sometimes had hard problems at work, mostly about coding and new bugs. When I could not fix them by myself, I had to search on Google or ask my team lead. But now, I don't have many big problems anymore, because AI supports me very strongly."

Question 3: Communication with Team & PM when stuck

Interviewer: "When you face a problem and you cannot resolve it by yourself, how will you communicate with your team or your PM?"

Your Answer:

"First, I always try to fix the problem by myself for 1 or 2 hours. If I still cannot fix it, I will ask my teammates first. If they cannot help me, I will talk to my team lead or technical expert. At the same time, I also tell my PM early so we can find a solution together and not miss the deadline."

Question 4: Time Management & Tracking Multiple Deadlines

Interviewer: "How do you manage your daily task and keep track on this task when you have multiple deadlines? Are you good at time management skills? Can you give me a specific example?"

Your Answer:

"Yes, I think I manage my time well. Whenever I get a new task, I always write it down in my personal notebook. It records all tasks and deadlines for the day so I know what I need to finish. When I finish a task, I check it off. At the end of the day, I review my list to check for any missing work. If a task is delayed or I have too much work, I will proactively tell my team lead or client to find another solution."

Question 5: Working Overtime (OT)

Interviewer: "Do you have to work overtime a lot? Are you willing to do that or because the manager requires you to do that?"

Your Answer:

"In the past, I had to work overtime a lot, but now I don't. Normally, I try to finish my work during office hours. If a delay is my fault, I am willing to work overtime to fix it. However, if the task has a problem or the scope is too big, I will report it to my manager first so we can arrange it. But if my manager still requires me to OT for the project, I am always willing to do it."

Question 6: Future Goals (3–5 years)

Interviewer: "What is your target or your goal in the next three or five years? What do you want to achieve?"

Your Answer:

"In the next 3 to 5 years, my goal is to become a Technical Lead. To achieve this, I want to learn new programming languages and get official OutSystems certifications. Especially, I want to develop strongly in AI engineering to catch up with new technology trends. At the same time, I am also improving my English skills every day to work better in international projects."

Question 7: Biggest Strength

Interviewer: "Can you share with me one of the most strengths that you are confident about yourself?"

Your Answer:

"I think my biggest strength is my strong business analysis skill. I have experience working on very complex systems, such as tax and logistics projects. Because of this, I can understand requirements very fast and build the right solution. Another strength is my independence. I can work very well by myself and handle tasks smoothly from start to finish."


"AI helps me with almost everything in the project. It helps me analyze business requirements, write code, test, and fix bugs. I just need to give clear prompts and instructions to the AI, and then I review and test the final result carefully to make sure everything is correct


First, I read through all the requirements and write down the main points. Then, I break down the features into smaller functions to make them easier to read and clear them one by one. If anything is unclear, I will directly ask the BA or team lead to get the right answer
